<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luganda</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ganda language</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luganda is the Bantu language of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baganda">Baganda</a> of central Uganda. It is spoken as a first language by several million people and as a second language by many more, making it the most widely spoken indigenous language of Uganda. It was written in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> alphabet by missionaries from the 1870s, and a substantial literature, including histories of Buganda's kings, appeared from around 1900.</p></div>
